X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute
DTSTART:20260927T000000Z
DTEND:20260927T010000Z
LOCATION:The historic Bur Oak tree in front of the IMU\, by Dunn Meadow j
 ust off 7th Street
SUMMARY:Listening to and with Trees: A Full Moon Deep Listening Sound Gat
 hering
DESCRIPTION:The Tree School Presents… Listening to and With Trees: A Fu
 ll Moon Deep Listening and Sound Gathering with Composer and Harpist Gabr
 iel Jenks  We welcome you to the first in our series of being with trees 
 at night.  Step away from the noise and tune into the nocturnal rhythm of
  the 180-year-old Bur Oak.&#160\;  Beneath its majestic canopy\, we will 
 begin the evening with a series of guided deep listening practices\, open
 ing our awareness to each other and the teaching presence of the tree.  A
 s we settle in and the full moon begins to rise\, award-winning Jacobs Sc
 hool of Music composer and musician Gabriel Jenks (https://music.indiana.
 edu/faculty/current_adjunct/jenks-gabriel.html) will improvise on the har
 p a real-time soundscape in collaboration with the moon\, the tree\, the 
 night\, and all of us together.  Come dream\, imagine\, listen\, and rest
 ore.What to Bring  A favorite blanket\, yoga mat\, or chair to listen com
 fortably on the ground. Bring an open heart\, big ears\, and a desire to 
 rest deeply with the wisdom of the Bur Oak at night.Rain Policy  In the e
 vent of inclement weather\, this event will be rescheduled. Registered gu
 ests will receive an update via email at 4:00 PM on the day of the event.
  Registration is not required\, though much appreciated.&#160\;Contact  A
 ny questions? Reach out to Catherine Bowman (cabowman@iu.edu (mailto:cabo
 wman@iu.edu)) or Kaylie Fougerousse (kefouger@iu.edu (mailto:kefouger@iu.
 edu)).&#160\;Funded by IU Research through the Public Arts and Humanities
  Project.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>The Tree School Presents… Liste
 ning to and With Trees: A Full Moon Deep Listening and Sound Gathering wi
 th Composer and Harpist Gabriel Jenks</strong></p><p>  We welcome you to 
 the first in our series of being with trees at night.</p><p>  Step away f
 rom the noise and tune into the nocturnal rhythm of the 180-year-old Bur 
 Oak.&#160\;</p><p>  Beneath its majestic canopy\, we will begin the eveni
 ng with a series of guided deep listening practices\, opening our awarene
 ss to each other and the teaching presence of the tree.</p><p>  As we set
 tle in and the full moon begins to rise\, award-winning Jacobs School of 
 Music composer and musician <a href="https://music.indiana.edu/faculty/cu
 rrent_adjunct/jenks-gabriel.html">Gabriel Jenks</a> will improvise on the
  harp a real-time soundscape in collaboration with the moon\, the tree\, 
 the night\, and all of us together.<br />  Come dream\, imagine\, listen\
 , and restore.</p><p><strong>What to Bring</strong><br />  A favorite bla
 nket\, yoga mat\, or chair to listen comfortably on the ground. Bring an 
 open heart\, big ears\, and a desire to rest deeply with the wisdom of th
 e Bur Oak at night.</p><p><br /><strong>Rain Policy</strong><br />  In th
 e event of inclement weather\, this event will be rescheduled. Registered
  guests will receive an update via email at 4:00 PM on the day of the eve
 nt. Registration is not required\, though much appreciated.&#160\;</p><p>
 <br /><strong>Contact</strong></p><p>  Any questions? Reach out to Cather
 ine Bowman (<a href="mailto:cabowman@iu.edu">cabowman@iu.edu</a>) or Kayl
 ie Fougerousse (<a href="mailto:kefouger@iu.edu">kefouger@iu.edu</a>).&#1
