  26–28)\, and the mandatory December 12 orientation.    </p></li><li><p
  data-path-to-node="11\,2\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="11\,2\,0" data-i
 ndex-in-node="0">III. Housing &amp\; Classes:</strong> Guidance on the Ca
 pital Campus residency and the academic courses offered in D.C.    </p></
 li><li><p data-path-to-node="11\,3\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="11\,3\,
 0" data-index-in-node="0">IV. Ground Game:</strong> Peer-to-peer breakout
 s and alumni panel discussion on commuting\, and professional life in DC.
     </p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="13"><strong data-path-to-node="1
 3" data-index-in-node="0">Biography: Ambassador &amp\; Professor Lee Fein
 stein</strong></h3><p data-path-to-node="14">  Ambassador Lee Feinstein i
 s a Senior Managing Director and the President of McLarty Associates. He 
 previously served as the U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of Poland and he
 ld senior positions at the Department of State\, including Principal Depu
 ty Director and a Member of the Policy Planning Staff. He was the Foundin
 g Dean of the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies a
 t Indiana University from 2014 to 2022. Ambassador Feinstein is a member 
 of the Council on Foreign Relations and the American Academy of Diplomacy
 \, and holds a JD from Georgetown University Law Center.</p><p data-path-
 to-node="14">  &#160\;</p><p data-path-to-node="14"><em><strong>Can't mak
 e the full hour? No problem. This is a come-and-go strategy session desig
 ned to fit your Thursday schedule.</strong></em></p><p data-path-to-node=
 "14"><strong>Link to Application:</strong><a class="external" href="https
 ://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24aW">https://iu.co1.qualt
 rics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24a</a></p>
